<title>AUSTRALIA: Rural Property suspension lifted.</title>
<headline>Rural Property suspension lifted.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The suspension on Rural Property Trust's (RPT) units would be lifted from the start of trading on Wednesday after the completion of its unit holders meeting on Tuesday, the Australian Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>RPT's manager, Rural Asset Management (RAM), resigned before the meeting which was called by Bankers Trust International (BTI) to vote for RAM's removal.</p>
<p>BTI, which holds a 19.6 percent stake in RPT, requisitioned the meeting in March to depose RAM as manager, saying that RAM had &quot;demonstrated a poor track record of profitability&quot;.  </p>
<p>BTI said RAM had accepted a retirement payout of A$500,000 instead of the A$2.25 million it had sought.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
